<title>INDIA: India ABB up 2.2 pct at BSE after results.</title>
<headline>India ABB up 2.2 pct at BSE after results.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of electrical equipment maker Asea Brown Boveri (ABB) rose 12.0 rupees, or 2.19 percent, to 560.0 rupees at the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) in late afternoon trade on Monday, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The company on Friday announced a 147.7 percent jump in net profit to 1.55 billion rupees in calendar 1996 against 625.3 million the previous year.</p>
<p>ABB said its total income in 1996 climbed to 11.86 billion rupees, from 9.19 billion in 1995. At 1425 p.m. (0855 GMT), over 9,700 ABB shares were traded at the BSE.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
